    "title": "Chipotle offers BOGO deal for 'tattooed' guests today at 3 p.m.",
    "text": "March 13, 2026, 10:29 a.m. CTChipotle is offering a buy-one-get-one promotion for customers with tattoosThe promotion runs for one hour only, from 3 p.m. to 4 p.m. todayTemporary or drawn-on tattoos are also eligible for the deal at the staff's discretionThe offer is inspired by a social media trend comparing tattoos to Chipotle's to-go bagsFor one hour only, Chipotle will be treating its tattooed guests to a buy-one-get-one promotion today from 3 p.m. to 4 p.m. Even if you don’t have any permanent ink, the “tattoo can mean real, temporary, drawn-on, or another creative iteration invoking tattoos, as determined at the sole discretion of restaurant staff,” Chipotle’s website states.The promotion, titled “tatted like a Chipotle Bag BOGO,” plays off a viral Internet trend as well as leaning into the tradition of tattoo shops offering flash tattoo specials on Friday the 13th.The phrase “tatted like a Chipotle bag” is said to have originated with a 2019 social media post on X that compared Adam Levine’s patchwork tattoos to the pattern of a Chipotle to-go bag. People have made their own social media posts and videos since then, showing off their own Chipotle bag-esque tats.\"What started as an internet meme became a real-world expression of fandom for our brand,\" Stephanie Perdue, interim chief marketing officer, wrote in a statement.This will be the second year Chipotle has launched the promotion, with last year’s event driving the “highest-ever sales during the 3 to 4 p.m. non-peak hour,” Chipotle released in a statement.There are some ground rules, though: the free item is earned only with the purchase of a full-priced entrée of equal or greater value, not including kids’ meals. The cut-off is five free items per check and is only available in-store.What’s on the Chipotle menu?Chipotle is known for its fast-casual format of build-your-own burritos, tacos, bowls, salads and more.Some of Chipotle’s mainstay proteins include their chicken, steak, beef barbacoa, carnitas and sofritas (plant-based protein.)Right now, Chipotle’s Chicken Al Pastor, balancing heat, pineapple sweetness, fresh lime and cilantro, is back for a limited time.Chipotle also recently added a high-protein menu offering items with 15 to 81 grams of protein. Some of these high-protein options include the Double High Protein Bowl and High Protein-High Fiber Bowl.Where is my closest Chipotle?Luckily, Chipotle locations are plentiful. The brand had over 4,000 restaurants in operation at the end of 2025, Chipotle stated. In Escambia and Santa Rosa County, you can find Chipotles at the following locations:5100 N. Ninth Ave.3240 W. Michigan Ave.725 Gulf Breeze Parkway8870 Boesch Lane1674 E. Nine Mile Road8333 Mikajack Ave., Navarre4645 US-90, PaceFor a full list of locations or more menu information, visit Chipotle’s website at Chipotle.com.Hungry for more? Stay up to date on the latest restaurant news by subscribing to our free Pensacola Eats newsletter, delivered to your inbox every Wednesday. Sign up for the newsletter at profile.pnj.com/newsletter.",
